Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||02-16-2001||03:34 AM||||Hmmm, i have a fellow offering a Black 86 GT manual trans. The car seems to have everything, but a broken front marker light, and the battery cover/vent, however it could be in the trunk.  Anyway, the car needs a clutch, but the engine runs fine, however its not drivable at the moment due to the clutch, or so im told.  Im going to go have a look tommorow morning!  Oh, and the price?   $600,    it sounds good to me, i imagine in the condition it is in i could part it out and still make back that money if i never get around to fixing the car, Just looking for opinions!||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||02-16-2001||04:27 AM||||I say go for it........$600 is cheap and you can certainly recoup that if you had to part it out.  <P>If you're mechanically inclined you can replace the clutch itself for a few hundred dollars.  I would highly recommend installing a new master and slave cylinder (GM only!) along with the new clutch.  <P>If you need other stuff for it just post in the Mall section and someone will help you out.  I sell parts along with several other members, so most parts are just a click away.<P>Good luck! ||||reg||10
